WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.734
We begin with

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.402
important news just in to CNN.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:02.769
The debt

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.504
limit talks on Capitol Hill

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.106
hitting a snag this morning.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.707
The top Republican negotiator

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.975
walking out of a meeting

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.643
saying the White House stance

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.911
is unreasonable.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:12.979
Congressman Garrett Graves

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:16.016
says talks for now are, quote, on pause.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:17.450
That just a few hours

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.251
after President Biden

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.053
was briefed by his top negotiators

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.155
the president leaving a G7 leaders dinner

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.157
in Japan early for that update.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.359
And less than 24 hours ago,

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:26.960
Team Biden

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.028
and the Republican House Speaker

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:28.962
Kevin McCarthy

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.296
both voicing optimism

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.631
saying they were seeing progress

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.465
in those talks

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.701
so that one member of the centrist

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.303
Problem Solvers Caucus,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.005
everyone is not going to be happy

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:41.341
with everything that's to.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.242
Always a good deal

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.110
if everyone's a little upset

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:44.477
and you know

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.445
it's not going to be perfect.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.980
But the bottom line is we're going

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.414
to make sure

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.381
that the full faith and credit

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.449
United States continues

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.451
Let's get straight to

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.485
CNN's Melody and Ana.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.586
She's live on Capitol Hill.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.854
Melody, early in the morning,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.390
there was optimism. What happened?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.325
Well, this is a huge setback

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.226
for these talks.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.161
There was optimism,

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.395
as you noted, yesterday,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.230
even heading into this meeting.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.331
Negotiators did meet

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.133
this morning on Capitol Hill,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.202
but they briefly broke up

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.037
and coming out of that meeting,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:11.871
Garret Graves,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.039
one of the lead negotiators

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.041
for Republicans, told us we do.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.676
We decided to press pause

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.778
because it's just not productive.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.013
So I talked to some sources

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:20.346
who said

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:20.680
there are

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.915
a number of issues

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.715
where they just feel like

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.484
they're at an impasse right now.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.652
And as of right now,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.420
there are no additional meetings

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.822
scheduled for today.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.123
So, look, John,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.324
you've seen these negotiators

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.425
play out before.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.961
Usually there are legislative blowups

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:35.628
before everyone

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.263
can finally come together.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.965
There's a lot of posturing

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.200
that goes on in both sides.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.502
And as we've seen, both Republicans

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.703
and Democrats are facing

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.437
a lot of pressure

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.805
and getting a lot of heat from their

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:46.606
right and left

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.042
flanks to not cave and to dig in.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.911
But in terms of a timeline,

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.313
it is very problematic

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.115
because they were hoping to reach a deal

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.116
by this weekend.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.083
That is something that Speaker

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.318
Kevin McCarthy said

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:58.985
is needed

00:01:58.985 --> 00:01:59.252
in order

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.487
to get this bill through the floor

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.521
and get it over to the Senate

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.956
by this early June deadline.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.391
And so it is all but dashing hopes

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.993
that negotiators are going to be able

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:07.694
to reach a deal

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.095
in principle by this weekend.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:09.863
That's not to say that

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.764
they can't eventually get it done.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.133
But this is not a very welcome

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.901
development on Capitol Hill John.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.336
And Mel, any details?

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.138
Sometimes it's one little thing

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.072
that can set these things

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.106
off the rails for a little bit.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.641
Sometimes it's kind of a combination

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.642
that they're stuck on everything

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.344
and they just say, let's take a break.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.311
Do we know?

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.347
Yeah, I think it's more the latter.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.249
It's a combination of issues.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.984
The talks had been slowly

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.318
but surely moving ahead.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.153
Some of the issues

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.954
that have come up in the last 24 hours,

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.389
according to our sources.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:36.923
The White House here

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.558
in pushing for a debt ceiling hike

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.560
that would last into 2025

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.194
because they don't want

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.395
have to deal with this again

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.496
until after the next

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.430
presidential election.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.732
But in talking to Republicans

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:46.266
that is something

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.634
that if we're going to entertain that

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.301
we need to see

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.603
a lot more savings and cuts

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.938
put on the table.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.072
The other issue at play

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.140
has been work requirements.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:54.274
That's

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.942
something Republicans are pushing for.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.076
Biden seems to be open

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.344
to some form of work

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.279
requirements for Tanna,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.346
which is the Temporary Assistance

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.315
for Needy Families programs.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.816
But nothing has been finalized.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:04.884
So still a lot to go

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:05.952
and a lot that could go wrong

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.687
between now and early June John.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.821
Senator, appreciate the hustle

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.023
and the breaking news on Capitol Hill.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.991
Keep us posted if we learn anything else.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.759
With me in studio

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:13.593
to share their reporting

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.562
and their insights, CNN's Jeff Zeleny.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.463
Brianna Sotomayor of The Washington Post

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.999
and Joe, still in The New York Times.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.269
So this is both expected, I would say,

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.171
because the issues are so important

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.673
and the divide is so big.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.507
But also

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.975
potentially troubling

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:29.876
if you're a CEO,

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.311
if you're financial markets,

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.011
if you're the president,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.445
United States,

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.813
who's overseas right now

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.681
telling people,

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.783
I got this, America will not default

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.584
without question.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.418
I mean, all signs

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.652
had been pointed to an agreement,

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.119
which was actually

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.020
a little surprising

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.289
because that does not usually happen

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.257
sort of going into a weekend.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:47.193
But I think that one thing this is doing

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.094
We've only known about this

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:48.695
for a short time,

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.763
but already the sense of urgency,

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.131
I think perhaps from Wall Street

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.066
may change on this.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.968
We'll see what the market does today.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:55.835
But heading into the weekend,

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:57.270
this is not the place

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:57.904
where the White House

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.105
thought they would be.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:03:59.973
You heard the optimism

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.841
from Josh Gottheimer there,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.409
the congressman from New Jersey.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.410
So, look,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.545
this often happens

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.180
there are some hiccups,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.581
but it is the work requirements

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.749
that is causing the White House

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.651
a lot of grief from the left.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.419
And so that's the advice here

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.320
that they find themselves.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.622
And to that point, when you see

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:16.823
Josh Schottenheimer saying,

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:17.790
I think we're going to get there

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.458
and to get there still,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.692
when you see both the president

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.526
and the House speaker

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.362
saying we're suddenly making progress,

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.731
that's a conversation in the middle.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.366
And so both the left and the right say,

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.667
oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.868
And so let's start with the left.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.137
You have Democrat progressive saying,

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.472
stop negotiating, Mr.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.340
President, invoke the 14th Amendment.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.742
Never really been tested in the courts.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:36.609
But just say, you know,

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.444
the Constitution says the amendment says

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.846
the public debt can never be questioned.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.513
Bernie Sanders

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.748
among the progressives are saying,

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.383
we don't want cuts. Take a chance

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.620
Using the 14th Amendment

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.254
would allow

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.656
the United States to continue

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.357
to pay its bills on time

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.592
and without delay,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.627
prevent an economic catastrophe

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.128
and prevent

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.462
devastating cuts

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.130
to some of the most

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.165
vulnerable people in this country.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.968
It should be exercised if necessary.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.304
So, again, we go into the details.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.405
But if you're the White House team,

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.072
you're walking back

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:06.806
into the meeting today,

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.007
even though you're making progress.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.509
You know, the phones are lighting up

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.311
with progressives saying, stop.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.211
Don't give away too much.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.746
And they have been they have been. Right.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:13.980
I mean,

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.815
they've already been feeling the pressure

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.216
from the left flank,

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.118
particularly after last weekend

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.453
when the president cited

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:21.621
the fact that he did vote

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.456
for some work requirements as a senator

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.425
right before he left on his trip as well.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.026
He had comments where he said,

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:27.627
look, you know,

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.095
we're talking about work requirements,

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:29.796
but it wouldn't be of

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.130
anything of serious consequence.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.432
He has dropped hints

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:34.100
that that is a subject,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.001
a point of focus

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.235
now where there could be

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.236
possible consensus,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.772
which has led to a frustrated left

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.708
flank of the party at this point.

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:42.608
But remember,

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.143
in terms of using the 14th Amendment,

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:44.977
this is also somebody

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.646
and President Biden that came into office

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:47.113
and often

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.181
celebrated, talked

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.283
about his ability to strike deals

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.984
with members on the other side.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.119
So would you

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.887
when you look at that context

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.123
Is he really going to go for this option?

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.558
Green job here the other day

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.092
also said

00:05:59.092 --> 00:05:59.625
that he didn't think

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.561
that would be an ultimate solution

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.762
for what we're seeing. Right.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.930
They want to talk it out.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.131
And again, just yesterday,

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:05.732
the House speaker,

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.799
if you could put the negotiators

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:07.166
back up,

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.701
number one, Garret Graves is his trusted

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.969
deputy among House Republicans.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:10.536
But the House speaker

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.271
complimented the White House team saying,

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:12.939
I like these people,

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:13.706
I trust these people.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.674
We can get it done.

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.743
That sent a signal to McCarthy's right.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.243
And of course,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.778
he is just tenuously speaker of the House

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.079
Freedom Caucus yesterday

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.347
saying the US House of Representatives

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:22.382
has done its job.

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.883
There should be no further discussion

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.818
until the Senate passes legislation.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.321
So the speaker's right flank saying stop,

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.522
we don't like this. Nice talk.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:29.956
Yeah, it's

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.457
been a very interesting contrast

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.225
this entire week

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:34.060
because McCarthy has been using

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.762
every moment possible to say

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.929
things are going well.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.065
Look, all Republicans are united.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.100
He couldn't stop saying that on repeat,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.202
while at the same time behind the scenes

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.070
concern ratings

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.105
were starting to get pretty shaky.

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:48.374
They were worried at Garrett Graves

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:49.175
actually being tapped.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:49.675
They see him

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.377
as someone who is just a dealmaker.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.012
So they already had a feeling

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.081
that their bill that they passed,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:55.982
they know a lot of it

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.617
is not going to become law,

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.885
but they really did

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.219
do not see graves

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.188
as someone who could deliver

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:03.423
on a lot of what the freedom

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.123
caucus wants.

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:04.824
So this

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.359
statement that they put out yesterday

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.527
strategically

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:08.961
after they left, after even

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.430
they were being very complimentary

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.764
of where things are,

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.332
is really bigger

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.801
I think we should be looking at it more

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.068
as to what this means

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:16.869
for these next steps.

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.703
And clearly,

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:18.671
clearly, Graves

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:19.639
is now listening and saying,

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.973
maybe we should pause,

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.008
maybe we should pause.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:23.142
And now the question is is it

